  "body": "User request: a header template for the GitHub release page that links CHANGELOG.md, gives a shallow overview of what this release cut contains (not every release in history), points to the issues as the current roadmap, links https://solidcraft.io/discord for questions, points to issues for bug reports and feature/enhancement requests, and ends with a thank-you list of the release's contributors.\n\n- New `.github/RELEASE_TEMPLATE.md` with placeholders `{{VERSION}}`, `{{TAG}}`, `{{REPO_URL}}`, `{{NOTES}}`, `{{CONTRIBUTORS}}`.\n- `release.yml`: the notes step becomes \"Release page from the template\" - it keeps #92's guards (fails if RELEASE_NOTES.md has no `---`, starts with one, or its first section isn't the tag's version), drops the section's own title line, collects contributors as the distinct GitHub logins of commit authors between the previous `vX.Y.Z` tag and this one (`gh api compare`, bots dropped; a fallback line when none), fails if the template lost a placeholder, and writes `dist/release-body.md`.\n- Tested locally (Windows PowerShell) for v0.12.1 against the real repo: header, the 0.12.1 notes, report links and `- @NeoTech` render as expected.\n- Contributors are mentioned with `@login` (GitHub notifies them; that is the thank-you). Commits whose author has no GitHub account (e.g. Co-Authored-By trailers) are not listed.\n\nChangelog: none (CI only)",
